---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Second Bell"
  description="How Second Bell collects, uses and protects information about website visitors."
>
  <main class="privacy-page">
    <article>
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 6 August 2026</p>

        <p class="intro">
          Second Bell respects your privacy and aims to collect as little
          information about visitors as reasonably possible.
        </p>

        <p>
          This policy explains what information may be collected when you visit
          <a href="https://secondbell.co.uk">secondbell.co.uk</a>, why it is
          collected and how it is handled.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="operator">
        <h2 id="operator">Who operates this website?</h2>

        <p>Second Bell is operated by Tim O’Donnell.</p>

        <p>
          For questions about this privacy policy or how information is handled,
          contact:
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:YOUR-EMAIL@example.com"> YOUR-EMAIL@example.com </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="automatic-information">
        <h2 id="automatic-information">Information collected automatically</h2>

        <p>
          When you visit Second Bell, limited technical and usage information
          may be processed to deliver, secure and understand the performance of
          the website.
        </p>

        <p>This may include:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>the pages you visit;</li>
          <li>the approximate date and time of your visit;</li>
          <li>the website or search engine that referred you;</li>
          <li>your general country or region;</li>
          <li>your browser, operating system and device type;</li>
          <li>page-loading and website-performance information;</li>
          <li>
            technical information needed to detect malicious or automated
            traffic.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>This information is used to:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>provide and secure the website;</li>
          <li>understand which pages and articles are useful to readers;</li>
          <li>identify technical or performance problems;</li>
          <li>improve the design, content and accessibility of the website;</li>
          <li>
            identify and respond to misuse, attacks or other security threats.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Second Bell does not use website analytics to build individual visitor
          profiles or for targeted advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="analytics">
        <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>

        <p>Second Bell currently uses two analytics services.</p>

        <h3>GoatCounter</h3>

        <p>
          GoatCounter provides aggregate information about website visits,
          popular pages and referral sources.
        </p>

        <p>
          GoatCounter is designed to operate without advertising trackers and
          does not use cookies or browser storage to identify visitors. It does
          not provide Second Bell with visitors’ names, email addresses or
          complete IP addresses.
        </p>

        <p>
          Analytics information is used only to understand general readership
          patterns and improve the website.
        </p>

        <p>
          GoatCounter is operated from Ireland, with service data hosted in
          Finland and Germany.
        </p>

        <h3>Cloudflare Web Analytics</h3>

        <p>
          Cloudflare Web Analytics provides aggregate visitor and
          website-performance information, including page views, referral
          sources, approximate country, device type and Core Web Vitals.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cloudflare Web Analytics is designed to collect limited performance
          and usage data without tracking visitors across different websites.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cloudflare also processes technical traffic information as part of
          hosting, delivering and protecting Second Bell.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="cookies">
        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

        <p>
          Second Bell does not currently set advertising cookies or use cookies
          to track visitors across different websites.
        </p>

        <p>
          GoatCounter does not place analytics cookies or use local storage in
          visitors’ browsers.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cloudflare may use essential security technologies where necessary to
          protect the website, manage malicious traffic or provide Cloudflare
          services. These are used for website operation and security rather
          than advertising.
        </p>

        <p>
          This section will be updated if Second Bell introduces features that
          use additional cookies or browser-storage technologies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="email-contact">
        <h2 id="email-contact">Contact by email</h2>

        <p>
          If you contact Second Bell by email, the information you provide may
          include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>your name;</li>
          <li>your email address;</li>
          <li>the content of your message;</li>
          <li>any other information you choose to include.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          This information will be used to read, manage and respond to your
          enquiry.
        </p>

        <p>
          Email correspondence will normally be retained only for as long as it
          is reasonably needed to deal with the enquiry and any related
          follow-up. It may be retained for longer where necessary to establish
          a record of correspondence, meet a legal obligation or resolve a
          dispute.
        </p>

        <p>
          Please do not send confidential, sensitive or unnecessary personal
          information by email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="future-features">
        <h2 id="future-features">Forms, comments and mailing lists</h2>

        <p>
          Second Bell does not currently operate visitor accounts, public
          comments, a newsletter mailing list or a website contact form.
        </p>

        <p>
          This policy will be updated before any such feature is introduced.
        </p>

        <p>
          Where a form is added, a short privacy explanation will also be
          displayed at the point where personal information is collected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="lawful-basis">
        <h2 id="lawful-basis">Lawful basis for processing</h2>

        <p>
          Where UK data-protection law applies, information may be processed on
          the following bases.
        </p>

        <h3>Legitimate interests</h3>

        <p>
          Limited website analytics and security information may be processed
          where it is reasonably necessary to:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>operate and protect the website;</li>
          <li>measure aggregate website use;</li>
          <li>understand which content is useful;</li>
          <li>improve the website’s performance and accessibility.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          These activities are designed to minimise the collection of
          identifiable information.
        </p>

        <h3>Consent</h3>

        <p>
          Where consent is required for a future feature, such as an optional
          mailing list or non-essential tracking technology, visitors will be
          asked for consent before that processing takes place.
        </p>

        <h3>Legal obligations</h3>

        <p>
          Information may be processed where necessary to comply with a legal
          obligation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="recipients">
        <h2 id="recipients">Who receives information?</h2>

        <p>
          Information may be processed by service providers used to operate
          Second Bell, including:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts, delivers, protects and
            measures the performance of the website;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>GoatCounter</strong>, which supplies privacy-focused website
            analytics;
          </li>
          <li>the provider used to receive and store email correspondence.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          These providers process information only as required to provide their
          respective services and are subject to their own privacy and security
          arrangements.
        </p>

        <p>
          Second Bell does not sell visitors’ personal information to
          advertisers or data brokers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="international-processing">
        <h2 id="international-processing">International processing</h2>

        <p>
          Some service providers may process information in, or make it
          accessible from, countries outside the United Kingdom.
        </p>

        <p>
          Where personal information is transferred internationally, the
          relevant provider is responsible for using appropriate legal
          safeguards for those transfers.
        </p>

        <p>
          GoatCounter states that its hosted service stores data in Finland and
          Germany. Cloudflare operates a global network and may process
          technical website traffic through infrastructure in different
          countries.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention">
        <h2 id="retention">Retention</h2>

        <p>
          Second Bell retains information only for as long as it is reasonably
          needed for the purpose for which it was collected.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Aggregate analytics information may be retained to compare website
            traffic and performance over time.
          </li>
          <li>
            Technical security information is retained according to Cloudflare’s
            applicable service settings and retention periods.
          </li>
          <li>
            Email enquiries are normally deleted when they are no longer needed,
            subject to any legal, administrative or dispute-related reason for
            retaining them.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Because analytics platforms may apply their own retention
          arrangements, their retention periods may differ from those controlled
          directly by Second Bell.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="rights">
        <h2 id="rights">Your data-protection rights</h2>

        <p>
          Depending on the circumstances, UK data-protection law may give you
          rights including:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            the right to be informed about how your personal information is
            used;
          </li>
          <li>the right to request access to your personal information;</li>
          <li>the right to request correction of inaccurate information;</li>
          <li>the right to request deletion of information;</li>
          <li>the right to restrict certain processing;</li>
          <li>the right to object to certain processing;</li>
          <li>
            the right to receive information in a portable format where
            applicable;
          </li>
          <li>
            the right to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          These rights do not apply in every situation, particularly where no
          identifiable personal information is held.
        </p>

        <p>To make a request, contact:</p>

        <p>
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:YOUR-EMAIL@example.com"> YOUR-EMAIL@example.com </a>
        </p>

        <p>
          You may be asked for enough information to confirm your identity and
          locate any relevant records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="complaints">
        <h2 id="complaints">Complaints</h2>

        <p>
          Please contact Second Bell first if you have a concern about how your
          information has been handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          You also have the right to raise a concern with the UK Information
          Commissioner’s Office, the independent regulator responsible for data
          protection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="external-links">
        <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>

        <p>Second Bell contains links to other websites.</p>

        <p>
          Second Bell is not responsible for the privacy practices, content or
          security of external websites. You should review the privacy policy of
          any external service you visit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="children">
        <h2 id="children">Children’s information</h2>

        <p>
          Second Bell is written for a general audience interested in teaching
          and career change. It is not intended to collect personal information
          directly from children.
        </p>

        <p>
          Children should not submit personal information through email or any
          future website feature without the involvement of a parent, carer,
          teacher or other appropriate adult.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="security">
        <h2 id="security">Security</h2>

        <p>
          Reasonable technical and organisational measures are used to protect
          the website and any information handled through it.
        </p>

        <p>These measures include:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>HTTPS encryption;</li>
          <li>Cloudflare security and traffic protection;</li>
          <li>restricted access to website and service accounts;</li>
          <li>security headers;</li>
          <li>dependency and build checks;</li>
          <li>account security controls.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          No internet service or method of electronic storage can be guaranteed
          to be completely secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>

        <p>
          This policy will be reviewed periodically and updated when the
          website, analytics services or information-handling practices change.
        </p>

        <p>
          The date at the top of this page shows when the policy was last
          updated.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 24px 88px;
  }

  article {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 48px 0 16px;
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
  }

  .updated {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    color: var(--date-text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 24px;
  }

  li {
    margin: 8px 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--brick);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--marker);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 44px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .privacy-page {
      padding: 40px 20px 64px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
